1
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:03,080
Please insert coins.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,270
Whoa!

3
00:00:06,353 --> 00:00:07,183
Check it out!

4
00:00:07,266 --> 00:00:09,119
Look at all that juicy ocean water!

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:11,249
That's Director Scorching.

6
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:13,300
He's the epitome of extra.

7
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,837
How does she lug this around
without throwing out her back?

8
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,517
That's child's play for someone
with the blessing of weight.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,660
What even is that?

10
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,517
Basically, it means she can alter
the weight of anything she touches.

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,677
She can make stuff lighter or
heavier whenever she wants.

12
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,407
Makes hauling junk a breeze.

13
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:39,177
So I take it you refused
Captain Carriol's invitation

14
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,897
and disappeared into the
ocean to get away from him?

15
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:44,520
That's correct, but it's lame.

16
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:47,777
I was hunkered down on a
nice island. Till that...

17
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:50,417
Is there some special
reason you were hunkered?

18
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,780
I was waiting for him
to return to my side.

19
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:54,970
Who's the guy?

20
00:00:55,053 --> 00:00:57,667
Don't tell me it's that
bastard who left you!

21
00:00:57,940 --> 00:00:59,520
Some clams never learn.

22
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,160
Don't say that.

23
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,600
It's not true.

24
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,649
I know in my heart
he'll come back one day.

25
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,060
He will.

26
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,260
He'll return to pity.

27
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:10,877
I've got to be patient.

28
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,457
That's all there is to it!

29
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,757
Clinging to the memory of a man
who abandoned her without remorse,

30
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,057
she's deluded herself into believing
they'll see each other again.

31
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:20,552
But it's just a fantasy.

32
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,697
Also, that loser was a
bonafide marriage fraudster.

33
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:28,133
But she refuses to believe us no matter
how many times we try to tell her.

34
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,300
Oh, I've seen her.

35
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:37,080
When the captain came
to invite me, I'm sure.

36
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:42,620
That's Sulrin, a snow spirit like Kikoyu
whose allegiance lies with the Netherlord.

37
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,257
The snowstorms she conjures
are no laughing matter.

38
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:49,037
We're gonna have our work cut out for
us without Kikoyu around to back us up.

39
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,980
No joke.

40
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,137
That's exactly why Director Bear sent
someone along to aid the mission.

41
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:56,997
It's been a dog's age since I've
been to the Dog Mountain Stratum,

42
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,557
but it doesn't hold a candle
to the scorching sand.

43
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:02,217
Let's be real, it's
lukewarm and best out here!

44
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,182
I'm starting to think this was
some cruel prank, care of the bear.

45
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:09,137
Meekaboo, are you getting
enough nutrition in that thing?

46
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,926
Some food would cheer you up.

47
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,360
Somebody help me!

48
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,300
Whoa, a living drum kit!

49
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,497
This guy's the life of the party!

50
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:19,137
You can give me a kid if you don't!

51
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:22,197
Those two are about as
compatible as fire and water.

52
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,110
Here we

53
00:02:23,193 --> 00:02:30,140
go.

54
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,380
Oh

55
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,110
That's it.

56
00:03:23,193 --> 00:03:24,023
I want to go home.

57
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,355
It's scary out there.

58
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,580
He poured fuel on the flame
of her shut-in tendencies.

59
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,160
Time to step in.

60
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,480
Hello, Pity.

61
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:36,680
It's Pity.

62
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:37,880
What's up?

63
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:43,020
You went, sir-um-sir-what-eeks.

64
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,200
So, um, that was good.

65
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,560
Thanks a lot

66
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,300
You too?

67
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,480
Sir, thank you very much

68
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,477
What a peculiar magic item.

69
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:02,280
You're a real person, I can already tell.

70
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,997
Who would have thunk a
clam in a vending machine

71
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:07,197
would get along so well
and yet here we are?

72
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,162
I'm just glad I managed
to cheer her up a little.

73
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:11,702
I'm a nuisance.

74
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,394
I cause trouble for everyone around me.

75
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,461
And that especially goes for him.

76
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:20,500
I know he's a liar, but I still
can't bring myself to let go.

77
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:23,140
I'm so self-centered, aren't I?

78
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:25,240
A truly terrible person.

79
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:31,100
Well, it could be you earned
for instance if you went.

80
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,260
Thing is, I'm only good at defense.

81
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:39,320
You think they'd want
someone like me around? Yes.

82
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,700
I'm the evil evil.

83
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,440
You believe in me?

84
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:53,200
Well then, maybe I'll
try just a bit harder.

85
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:56,600
The clam is emerging from her shell.

86
00:04:57,660 --> 00:05:00,719
Oh, you gotta come taste
that salty sea air with me.

87
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,977
Not sure that's going to
help her want to open up,

88
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,589
but that combo is a
pretty darn good start.

89
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:12,577
Over there that's my
island it's still too far

90
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,337
away to really see
anything we can do better

91
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:20,077
than that form change tourist destinations

92
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:23,397
often have binocular
rentals i know they're

93
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,437
not packaged goods but i've been able to

94
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,797
change into service
machines since reaching rank

95
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,057
two i could wax poetic about the different

96
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:32,787
types but we're short
on time so i'll refrain

97
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:37,300
wow everything's crystal clear

98
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:39,737
Isn't that...

99
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:42,100
Pretty sure I see the fool's boat.

100
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,560
I'm back.

101
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:52,097
Hey, I was starting to worry about you?

102
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:54,298
What's with the makeshift entourage?

103
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:57,937
Heavy cast an illusion on us
to protect our identities.

104
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:01,340
Now we're total strangers
and an adorable kitty.

105
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:02,997
Oh, right.

106
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,577
The sea monsters, they've
been causing trouble.

107
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:08,820
So I hired bodyguards. Good thinking.

108
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:11,808
You need all the offensive
help you can get.

109
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:13,880
Come on.

110
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,480
Join our party, Pity.

111
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,317
It's going at a snail's pace.

112
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:20,988
Conquering the dungeon would be
a breeze with you on defense.

113
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,777
I'm waiting for him to come back.

114
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,200
So I can't go?

115
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,117
Well, we only ask that
you give it some thought.

116
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,717
Once this dungeon is handled,
we'll do what we can to help you.

117
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,517
We'll even help you track
down your long-lost lover.

118
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,580
Are you in?

119
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,760
Sorry. Still a no.

120
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,180
I can't go with you. I refuse.

121
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,280
Had a feeling you'd say that.

122
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,460
Way too bad.

123
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,780
We'd better step outside.

124
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:54,061
I'd hate to wreck your little house
by starting a nasty brawl here.

125
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,140
I breach.

126
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:56,650
Really?

127
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:58,730
Boxxo?

128
00:06:58,813 --> 00:06:59,643
What do you know?

129
00:06:59,726 --> 00:07:01,129
Seems the gang's all here.

130
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:06,757
Say, how about we indulge in some booze
while we work through our differences?

131
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:09,037
I wouldn't mind some of Bokso's finest.

132
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:12,897
We miss his deep-fried meats and
delightfully fizzy drinks so much it hurts.

133
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:13,921
Don't we, Shiro?

134
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,637
Just thinking about it
makes me hungry and thirsty.

135
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:19,520
It feels like it's been
forever, doesn't it?

136
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,497
Don't you dare look at me
with those wistful eyes.

137
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:25,521
In case you've forgotten,
we're enemies at the Mo.

138
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:28,020
It's too late.

139
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:31,040
They're clearly jonesing to fight. I know.

140
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,660
La-I-X-R-E-T.

141
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,050
Yeah.

142
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:39,397
We surveyed a hundred people
in the Clearflow Lake Stratum

143
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:42,715
and asked what they think of
Captain Carriol's actions.

144
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:47,077
Lamas and I collected a
few choice opinions about

145
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:50,042
the Menagerie of Fools
for just such an occasion.

146
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,240
First question.

147
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,257
What do you think of them working for the

148
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,777
Netherlord in order to
help a child in need?

149
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:58,477
They had three options
they could choose from.

150
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:01,240
Forgivable, unforgivable, and undecided.

151
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,345
Twelve people said forgivable.

152
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,220
Sixty said unforgivable.

153
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,660
And twenty-eight said undecided.

154
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,877
That's not nearly as
bad as I was expecting.

155
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:13,777
The people who said forgivable
had something in common.

156
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,077
They all said things like,

157
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:18,897
it's possible I would do the same thing
if I thought it would help my child.

158
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:22,217
Or, as a parent, I can't judge
without knowing the details.

159
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,600
Sounds tragic. Next question.

160
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:28,677
Do you think Filmina both deserves and
could do a lot better than Captain Carioid?

161
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,590
Hold on a sec.

162
00:08:29,673 --> 00:08:31,697
There's no reason to
read that one out loud.

163
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:34,517
Don't judge stuff when she's
getting in the good stuff.

164
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,835
You're gonna have to hold him tighter.

165
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,580
62 said definitely.

166
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,220
16 said perfect mismatch.

167
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,000
And 22 said hope he dies. That's rude.

168
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,877
What are those the choices anyway?

169
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,960
Everyone seems to be in agreement.

170
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,130
Interesting.

171
00:08:49,213 --> 00:08:52,777
Perhaps I should have searched longer
to find a more suitable husband.

172
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,660
Now for the final question.

173
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,297
If they ever came back and
apologized and accepted punishment,

174
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:00,880
would you forgive them?

175
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:04,620
The moment of truth has arrived.

176
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,135
It's the whole reason we went polling.

177
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:10,200
Twenty said I couldn't.

178
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:13,640
And eighty said I'd forgive them.

179
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:20,037
That result isn't all that
surprising when you think about it.

180
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:23,717
This whole time, they've been
focused on clearing the lowest floor,

181
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,976
so they haven't directly hurt anyone.

182
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:30,497
Besides, the folks in the Clear Flow
Lake Stratum are kind and open-minded.

183
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:35,168
I mean, seriously, they learned to embrace
a freaking talking vending machine.

184
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:38,032
I'll give you a sample of what they said.

185
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:41,777
They should have known that we would have
had their backs if they were in trouble.

186
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:44,257
If they weren't so stupid, we
could have pitched in to help.

187
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:45,170
There's more!

188
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,960
Just come back already.

189
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,575
Pay for the booze and we'll let it go.

190
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:53,637
It's the most natural thing in the world
for a parent to want to protect their kid.

191
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:57,477
But it's important to remember that
every action has a ripple effect.

192
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,089
Is this what your child
would want for you?

193
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:03,517
I'd be happy to knock some sense
into those empty heads of theirs.

194
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:06,077
So tell those whippersnappers
to hurry back!

195
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:09,977
If I had to guess, I'd say those
last two are Yumite and Shimelai.

196
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:11,060
Knowing them,

197
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,357
I bet they're filled with
regret for not realizing

198
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:16,322
how much the captain and
his wife were suffering.

199
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,190
Figures.

200
00:10:18,273 --> 00:10:19,103
Should've known.

201
00:10:19,186 --> 00:10:20,016
They're all busy-bodied.

202
00:10:20,099 --> 00:10:22,397
Oh, and here's one for
you from Miss Shirley.

203
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,397
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

204
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,997
I think we've heard
enough for today, Lamas.

205
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,197
No need to read that one.

206
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:29,997
Captain, you've got a record-setting
tab, so please come and pay it.

207
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:34,717
The young ladies of our fine establishment
miss your company, as well as that of Mr.

208
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,630
Akka and Mr.

209
00:10:35,713 --> 00:10:36,543
Shiro.

210
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,900
So, don't keep us waiting. XOXO!

211
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:41,740
Care to explain yourself?

212
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,517
You can tell what it sounds like.

213
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,177
The boys were curious about the place.

214
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:51,577
They practically dragged me, kicking and
screaming, so they could have a peek.

215
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:53,417
I didn't really have a
choice in the matter.

216
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:54,912
Tell her the truth, Dad.

217
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:57,657
You're the one who made us promise
not to tell Mom about our field trip.

218
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,717
It was your idea, and you kept
bragging about how you're a regular.

219
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,417
I'm sure your drinks were more enjoyable
with pretty ladies by your side.

220
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,977
I bet you had the time of
your life there, didn't you?

221
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:10,720
I should probably intervene
before things get violent.

222
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:19,100
Well, it's pretty obvious
who's behind this attack.

223
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:22,890
Weird.

224
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:23,840
She's not alone.

225
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,317
Have you finished blabbing
about your feelings?

226
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:30,077
I certainly hope you're not
considering betraying the Netherlord.

227
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:30,990
Of course not.

228
00:11:31,073 --> 00:11:32,337
I wouldn't dream of it.

229
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:34,655
The debt we owe is too steep for that.

230
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:37,637
It's been a blast, but the reunion's over.

231
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:40,517
What does he mean he owes
the Netherlord a debt?

232
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,541
I'd love to stay and chat
about the good old days.

233
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:48,657
If we had crossed paths sooner, things
may have turned out differently.

234
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,660
It's too late.

235
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,037
We've gone past the point of no return.

236
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,300
I'm truly sorry.

237
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:55,340
Yeah, me too. Really.

238
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,718
That's how it goes.

239
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,842
What are you even talking about?

240
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,657
I'm sure we can find a
way to save your son,

241
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:04,916
even without asking the
stupid Netherlord to help out!

242
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:12,377
You're so naive it's amusing you think
they're still worried about saving their son.

243
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:15,417
I'm happy to report that's not
a concern of theirs anymore.

244
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:21,400
What are you saying it's time
for show and tell it can't be.

245
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:25,720
That's the captain's son.

246
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:34,157
Boxo boxo boxo i'm taking excellent
care of his darling little boy.

247
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:36,897
so there's no longer any
need to remove the curse.

248
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:40,717
I have taken it upon myself to
relieve this sweet child of his pain.

249
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,760
Since when can you remove curses?

250
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:44,667
Is that a snow spirit thing?

251
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:48,497
Beheading a snow spirit who
has blossomed into adulthood

252
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:51,698
transforms them into a statue
that can remove curses.

253
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:56,665
But what do you suppose happens if one
manages to keep her head on her shoulders?

254
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:01,897
The ability to remove curses is a
talent that is inherent to my kind.

255
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:05,480
As we mature, our abilities
continue to grow along with us.

256
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:08,577
The only catch is that the
target must remain near.

257
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:13,680
If you attempt to pry this child from my
grasp, his excruciating pain will return.

258
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,817
So basically you're holding a kid hostage.

259
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,400
This boy isn't a hostage.

260
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:22,237
I'm saving the captain's precious
son from a wretched existence.

261
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:26,217
This family wishes to satisfy my
every whim as a show of gratitude.

262
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:27,677
She's exactly right.

263
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:30,177
So I'm afraid we have no
choice but to serve the

264
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:33,217
Netherlord and fight to clear
the dungeon on his behalf.

265
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:37,497
You've made your choice, and nothing
we say could make you change your mind.

266
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:40,817
Unfortunately, the only option
left to us is to use force.

267
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:43,057
You're just another sad Netherlord crony.

268
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,857
Don't expect a shred of mercy.

269
00:13:44,940 --> 00:13:46,705
Love makes fools of all of us.

270
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:50,900
But hurting others, even for
love, that's just despicable.

271
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:54,660
I can't help but notice
your short one-snow spirit,

272
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,337
meaning none of you are
capable of stopping me.

273
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:00,280
from turning everyone
standing here to ice.

274
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:01,440
Not so fast.

275
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,517
This is kind of personal,
so why not let us handle it?

276
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,835
Don't be such a fool.

277
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:09,160
Unless you mean to defy me.

278
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,150
That's enough!

279
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,720
How can you be so cruel?
That was stupid! I'm sorry!

280
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,572
Let's just make it stop!

281
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:27,556
Better than I think it's
about time we end this farce.

282
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:31,060
I'm going to kill every
last one of you. How rude!

283
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,937
We'd better split up so she can't
hit us all at the same time.

284
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,397
I've had enough to hear
with your dirty tricks!

285
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:40,217
If the people fighting aren't getting
fired up, it's not a real battle!

286
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:41,960
Are you an actual imbecile?

287
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:46,847
You thought it was a good idea to charge
a snow spirit without any forethought?

288
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,900
That was barely looked warm.

289
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:53,140
Snow spirits are lame.

290
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,557
You're all cold as ice and boring to boot.

291
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:58,237
I would have assumed your
race already died off.

292
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,732
You're a true annoyance.

293
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,100
A flame spirit.

294
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:05,817
How come no one gave us the heads-up,
Director Scorching's a flame spirit?

295
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,940
Did you know, Hewleby? I did.

296
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:11,997
I also know their powers are essentially
the opposite of the snow spirits.

297
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,357
As you might have guessed?

298
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,317
They can control fire
and can be a bit hot.

299
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:18,040
A Snow Spirit's natural enemy.

300
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:20,713
Their people have fought countless wars.

301
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:24,097
That explains why Director
Vare chose him for the job.

302
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:25,062
It's brilliant!

303
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:28,420
With flame powers, he can go
toe-to-toe with Soul Ream!

304
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,050
Hmph.

305
00:15:30,133 --> 00:15:32,822
Ice Queen's mine, so sit
back and enjoy the show.

306
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,820
This measly battleground's
not gonna cut it!

307
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,237
Guess there's no use to
laying the inevitable captain.

308
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,817
This time will be different than the last.

309
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,637
I'm dead serious about
walking away the victor.

310
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,838
Things are about to get interesting.

311
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:56,317
I request to be the one to do it.

312
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,277
Quite the compliment.

313
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,957
Then I'll focus on the vice captain.

314
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,077
I'll beat up his stupid Osprey.

315
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:05,217
I'm not stupid, you loudmouthed loser!

316
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,130
Yeah, loser!

317
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:10,780
Children, it seems the time has
come to reveal our true forms.

318
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,500
She has wings?

319
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:20,505
The vice-captain has vamp fiend
blood flowing through her veins.

320
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,702
Aw, that's kinda badass, though.

321
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:31,397
Gotta say, with those wings, she looks
more like a fallen angel than a vampire!

322
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:34,097
Shall we let the battle begin?

323
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:36,440
Let's go!

324
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:44,797
So Filmina exploded.

325
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,497
So what am I supposed to do now?

326
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:47,977
You didn't explode anyone.

327
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:50,217
She conjured a water double to trick you.

328
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,577
The real her is there.

329
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:55,277
That was a noble effort.

330
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:58,500
Your bemusing attacks are
You're absolutely fearsome.

331
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:00,954
Too bad for you, I can simply fly away.

332
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:02,280
Good thinking!

333
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:06,920
We didn't used to have a way to fight
airborne enemies, but that was then.

334
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:08,690
Boom!

335
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:10,637
Check out this transformation!

336
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,661
The coin locker!

337
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,060
It's OWN!

338
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:17,674
I went ahead and blocked these bottled
beauties from entering my barrier.

339
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:24,720
You forgot I can control water!

340
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:27,840
Yeah, that's not ordinary water.

341
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:30,589
I know I've felt this
slimy texture before.

342
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,577
It was back in the origin straddle.

343
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:33,880
You bet you have.

344
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:38,120
It's a lubricant, gently-scented
lotion. Oh, no. My wings.

345
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,440
That was good.

346
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:45,437
But I'm afraid you're still
no match for my water.

347
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,350
Whoa!

348
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,550
Nice!

349
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,380
That went surprisingly well.

350
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:52,730
Ah!

351
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,140
She's killing it!

352
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:04,040
Why must you attack poor Pity?

353
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,500
I get it.

354
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:08,960
The woman who stole my
man put you up to this.

355
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,800
Pity won't give in.

356
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:15,592
The battle just started and she's
already come up with her own head cannon.

357
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:21,000
Need backup?

358
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:22,717
That's scary.

359
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,917
It's starting to look like
we'll have to buy some

360
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,797
time until Dad or Sulream
can come and bail us out.

361
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:28,710
Well said.

362
00:18:28,793 --> 00:18:29,623
Let's go.

363
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:32,255
We can't defeat them if they run away.

364
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,581
Good thing I'm a vending machine.

365
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,620
I came prepared for anything.

366
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,440
How inspired.

367
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,177
I think I know what you're planning.

368
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:43,200
Lock it. Charge. Right.

369
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,100
Special delivery.

370
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:58,280
Not our best moment.

371
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:01,324
You can't defeat us with
a bevy of busty ladies.

372
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:02,870
Yeah...

373
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,260
How dare you! That's cheating!

374
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,480
Boxxo, that was gross.

375
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:10,180
Why am I the one who's in hot water?

376
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:19,697
Those eyes of yours,
they're quite troublesome.

377
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:20,797
Colour me impressed.

378
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:23,468
Guess I'm not getting
anything by you, am I?

379
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,940
If I'm reading the room correctly,

380
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:29,877
it seems his eye breach ability
does more than just break blessings.

381
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,977
I was feeling pretty confident
we would win this battle,

382
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:35,354
but you guys are making me work for it.

383
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:37,050
Not good.

384
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:41,813
I've got to stop the captain, even if
it means I have to play the villain.

385
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:47,837
I don't really like the sound
of this, but you got it.

386
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,300
Hey! I'm up.

387
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:51,382
Wait, what the heck is going on?

388
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,920
I love me some fizzy,

389
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:07,904
but do you think you can try to be a bit
more gentle with the execution next time?

390
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,767
Hold up, what are you doing?

391
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:11,830
Come on, now.

392
00:20:11,913 --> 00:20:12,816
Let's be reasonable.

393
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:16,057
Did you know they say when
someone is unconscious?

394
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:17,837
It's good practice to remove their shoes.

395
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:20,038
to ensure they don't get overheated?

396
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:20,980
Go heavy!

397
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:24,057
He already picked up on the
threat I'm trying to lay down.

398
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,964
I regret that I have no choice.

399
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,657
But I'm not unconscious, you know.

400
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:28,657
Are you serious?

401
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:31,780
I really hate being on this
side of a Boxxo battle.

402
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:33,240
Me too, bro.

403
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:35,000
The feeling is mutual.

404
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,479
Seriously, though.

405
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:42,100
I can't go all out with that brat around.

406
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,185
He does make this complicated.

407
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,077
It would be extremely hard
for anyone who isn't armed

408
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:50,197
with magic or special blessings
to fight in that dimension.

409
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,110
Oh, Captain.

410
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:55,051
I believe he's using Eye Breach
to cancel out the blizzard.

411
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:56,520
So that's it.

412
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:59,837
This must be the area of effect
for his Eye Breach power.

413
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:01,861
This fight is going nowhere fast.

414
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,380
What are you doing?

415
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,577
Stop goofing off and put out those flames.

416
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:07,760
Sorry, but I'm too far away.

417
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,480
You're completely useless.

418
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:12,700
We're in a dire situation.

419
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:18,087
He's moving close enough
to put out the fire.

420
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:21,540
And look, she's utterly
distracted at the moment.

421
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:24,097
This is our chance to
catch them off guard.

422
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:25,020
He's right.

423
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:28,340
We're pretty much doomed
if we don't act fast. Yes.

424
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:30,700
We need you to stay here, Boxo.

425
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:33,781
We can't risk taking Filmina
and the others along.

426
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:35,040
Hello there.

427
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:38,180
Try it.

428
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,480
She's gone.

429
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,819
I know I've seen this trick before.

430
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:48,725
It's just like when they ran away
in the scorching sand stratum.

431
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,580
Barrier! I preach.

432
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,300
Forgive me, Boxo.

433
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:54,740
Holy crap, Cap.

434
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:57,273
My vending senses are tingling like mad.

435
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:01,460
You're actually the one
we were after all along.

436
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,240
oh

437
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:42,950
Right.

438
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:51,690
Up.

439
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:58,590
Up. Up.

440
00:22:58,673 --> 00:23:04,068
Up.

441
00:23:04,151 --> 00:23:06,197
I'm waiting for you, I'm waiting for you?

442
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:09,680
I'm waiting for you to feel you.

443
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,117
Oh, it's a good idea!

444
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:14,780
I can't see you, I can't see you.

445
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:17,057
I can't see you, I can't see you.

446
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:18,640
I can't see you.

447
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:37,920
I look forward to serving you again.
